{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Unformed and void.</b> תֹּהוּ is a term of astonishment and desolation — that a person would be astonished and desolate at the בֹּהוּ in it." "<b>Unformed.</b> אשטורדי״שון בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>Void.</b> A term of emptiness and void." "<b>Over the face of the deep.</b> Over the face of the waters that are upon the earth." "<b>And the spirit of Elohim was hovering.</b> The Throne of Glory stands in the air and hovers over the face of the waters by the breath of the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, and by His utterance — like a dove hovering over the nest; אקוב״טיר בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French estordison, 'astonishment'", 4 "the la'az is Old French acoveter, 'to cover/brood'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:03.845785478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}